ouses  alongside the dike and also add some  simple footage on the floodplains and  the dike as well it's not something that  I really had any idea behind I just  looked at many of them in real life and  figured I generally just wanted to have  some trees alongside the road on the  dike and a couple of trees in the  floodplains and at least make them look  a little bit more interesting than just  empty grass with some grass patches this  is also something that I may want to  like come back to when I start a new  city because one of the reasons that I  feel I could do something better than  the city I have at the moment aside from  trying to not voice crack in my videos  is that the city's really built as a  sort of large-scale model  area but it's not so much focused on the  smaller scene so I  to get into decorating certain fields  with grass patches and small flowers  because it's more about the grander  scheme of things and this is actually  something I would like to perhaps not do  in the next city but really focus on  really small details rather than trying  to get a really large sort of realistic  area going because what I sort of feel I  lack in this city not necessarily  everywhere but in general I would like  to do more is focus on the smaller  scenes and making those picturesque  areas which is something that I didn't  get as in as much and you can probably  tell by the time-lapse as well since I  build a lot of things from a large from  a far away aerial perspective rather  than zooming out to get every single  detail perfectly it's more designed from  well yeah an aerial perspective in  general then trying to make it look good  in the details and from the ground up  which doesn't mean that I try to make  the city look like one of these top-down  design cities because that's definitely  not something that I like doing but I  try to get a large scale and I might  want to make these scale a bit smaller  for future cities just so I can put more  effort into 